abstract: >
  UCMuon (You See Muon!) is an open-source simulation suite for cosmic-ray
  muon generation, transport, and muography. It runs either locally through a
  browser-based graphical interface or as command-line executables on HPC
  clusters. It provides surface muon generation (eight spectrum models, three
  source geometries), seven transport engines (the native UCMuon-MC stochastic
  engine, MUSIC, Bethe-Bloch, PROPOSAL, PUMAS backward/forward Monte Carlo, a
  Python backward Monte Carlo, and DEM-based terrain ray-tracing for real
  field deployments), and a muographic density-inversion suite. Primary
  applications are volcano imaging and subsurface density monitoring. The
  MUSIC source code is not redistributed (see docs/MUSIC_FILES.md for how to
  obtain it); the PUMAS library is downloaded automatically by the installers.

